{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For by the very thing that they schemed against them</b> — its meaning is: by the thing that the Egyptians schemed against Israel, I know that He is greater than all elohim. And the reason for this is that HaShem decreed upon Israel, \"and they shall serve them, and they shall afflict them\" (Genesis 15:13), and there would not have been upon the Egyptians so great a punishment for this, but they schemed against them and intended to annihilate them from the world, as it says (Exodus 1:10), \"Come, let us deal wisely with him, lest he multiply,\" and he commanded the midwives to kill the sons, and he decreed upon them, \"Every son that is born, you shall cast him into the Nile\" (ibid. 22), and because of this there came upon them the punishment that destroyed them completely. And this is what He said, \"and also the nation that they shall serve, I will judge\" (Genesis 15:14), as I explained there (ibid., and above 12:42). Now HaShem saw their scheme and took vengeance upon them for the insolence of their heart. And Scripture likewise says, \"for you know that they schemed against them\" (Nehemiah 9:10) — for the punishment was because of the insolence they intended to commit against them. For HaShem sees into the heart and executes justice for the oppressed, and is an avenger and a master of wrath, and none can stay His hand. And Onkelos (Targum Onkelos on Exodus 18:11), who said, \"for with the plan that the Egyptians devised to condemn Israel, by it they were judged\" — he means to say that their punishment was for the drowning of the children in the Nile, which is not included in \"and they shall serve them, and they shall afflict them,\" and therefore He destroyed them in water."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:10:13.994654372Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}